From a6f12b529e22edc3feaedd11792db2ff19fd3862 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:07:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 59/77] arm64: dts: allwinner: h713: device tree for the HY300
 Pro

Same pattern and same reason as sun50i-h713-hy310.dts: an include of the bench
board's tree plus model and compatible, so that the two cannot drift and a boot
log names the board it is on. The tree carries OF_UPSTREAM, so the file lands
under dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/ and its name carries the "allwinner/"
prefix; there is no Makefile line to add.

Nothing board-specific is overridden, because nothing board-specific has been
measured: the one number known to differ is the DRAM clock, and that lives in
the defconfig. The panel is unknown beyond the declared project id 0x34, and no
tree describes the panel anyway -- the display coprocessor drives it from its
own tables.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts

diff --git a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..35f26a6d20d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
+/*
+ * "HY300 Pro" projector, reported in issue #1 of
+ * well0nez/allwinner-h713-linux by its owner. Nobody here has held one.
+ *
+ * Like the HY310's tree, this is an include of the bench board's rather than a
+ * copy, for the same reason: a board should boot a device tree named after
+ * itself, so that a boot log says which board it is running on instead of
+ * naming one nobody has built for. The DRAM clock that distinguishes this
+ * board (636 MHz) lives in configs/hy300_pro_defconfig, not here.
+ *
+ * What is *not* claimed by this file: the panel. It declares project id 0x34,
+ * and that is all that is known about its display -- resolution, timings and
+ * port count have never been read off it. No node here describes a panel in
+ * any case; the display coprocessor drives it from its own tables.
+ *
+ * Nothing else about this board has been measured as different from the bench
+ * board's tree, so nothing else is overridden. When something is measured, it
+ * belongs here.
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "MagCubic HY300 Pro";
+	compatible = "magcubic,hy300-pro", "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
